  "data": {
    "body": "You friend, mass \\textbf{M}, jumps from a crouched position to a vertical standing positon, such that their center of mass moves vertically upward through height \\textbf{h}. During this process, the point of contact between your friend's feet and ground is stationary. Your friend experiences a normal force $F_N$ acting upward at the point of contact between the feet and the ground. Your friend's change in translational kinetic energy of center of mass is $\\triangle K_{trans}$, the change in internal energy in the process is $\\triangle E_{int}$, and the change in kinetic energy due to the torso moving relative to the center of mass is $\\triangle K_{rel}$. \n\nAcceleration due to gravity \\textbf{g} is downward. Ignore air resistance. \n\nWhich of the following equations represents the energy principle of the \\textbf{Extended system} as applied to your friend from the initial to the final positions shown above?",
    "solution": [
      2
    ],
    "answerChoices": [
      {
        "id": "80c2a21a-8e8a-463a-83ab-82e4442f321f",
        "index": 0,
        "body": "$\\triangle$ $K_{trans}$ = ($F_N$ - Mg)h",
        "questionId": "3d524fb4-d86a-49c6-ac40-4be943937315",
        "stats": {
          "count": 13
        },
        "resources": []
      },
